<p class="lede">These terms apply to every Meridian Library membership.</p>

<h2>Borrowing</h2>
<p>Members may borrow up to twelve items at a time for a period of three weeks. Items may be
  renewed twice, provided no other member has reserved them. Reference materials, rare books and
  items held in the local studies collection may be consulted on the premises but not borrowed.</p>

<h2>Overdue items</h2>
<p>An item not returned by its due date accrues a charge of ten pence per day, to a maximum of the
  replacement cost of the item. Borrowing rights are suspended once outstanding charges exceed five
  pounds and are restored as soon as the balance is cleared.</p>

<h2>Damage and loss</h2>
<p>Members are responsible for items borrowed on their card until those items are returned. A member
  who loses or damages an item beyond ordinary wear is asked to pay the replacement cost.</p>

<h2>Conduct</h2>
<p>We ask that members respect the quiet areas on the first floor, and that food is not brought into
  the reading room. Staff may ask any person whose behaviour disturbs others to leave.</p>

<h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
<p>We review these terms annually. Members are notified of material changes by post or email at
  least one month before those changes take effect.</p>
